{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>In the Name [of]</b> — he whose reckonings are on high, and under [his] companion. He began to comment on the plain sense of the book of \"And He spoke\" <b>in the wilderness of Sinai.</b> To make known that Moses did not ascend Mount Sinai after the Glory was in the Tent of Meeting:" "<b>On the first day of the second month.</b> To arrange the standards, and how they would journey and how they would encamp on account of the Sanctuary, for on the twentieth of the second month they set out:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The opening phrase appears to be a liturgical or poetic invocation; its precise reference is uncertain. Read literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:51.437923882Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}